    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="1109" n="1097" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg1097"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">892.014/10–2946: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stanton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-31T17:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>866. Reurtel No. 1228 Oct 29.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d870-f1"/> Matter observers
                    disputed areas connection transfer will be determined Wash in protocol governing
                    transfer. Dept concurs your view promptest
                    withdrawal French officers and three civilians from disputed area until
                    determination observers question. Inform Brit Min.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d870-f1" n="11" xml:id="d870-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it gave Mr. Stanton’s view that the “only sure way guaranteeing no
                    incidents before territories are returned is for French officers and three
                    French civilians be withdrawn from Battambang forthwith. I also doubt that
                    French officers there will contribute to maintenance peace and order
                    Battambang.” (802.014/10–2946).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
